<title>INDIA: Indian zinc firm tenders for concentrate sale.</title>
<headline>Indian zinc firm tenders for concentrate sale.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run Hindustan Zinc Ltd (HZL) has issued a global tender for the sale of 40,000 metric tonnes of zinc concentrate, a company statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>The concentrate is from the company's Rampura Agucha mines containing approximately 54.5 percent zinc.</p>
<p>The tender closes at 1.00 p.m. (0730 GMT) on August 28, the statement said.</p>
<p>HZL is one of India's leading base metal producers.</p>
</text>
